      "source": "You can do this with a call to [`connect()`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Combine/ConnectablePublisher/connect()), or by using [`autoconnect()`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Combine/ConnectablePublisher/autoconnect()) to automatically connect when a subscriber attaches, as shown here:",
      "normalizedSource": "You can do this with a call to [`connect()`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Combine/ConnectablePublisher/connect()), or by using [`autoconnect()`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Combine/ConnectablePublisher/autoconnect()) to automatically connect when a subscriber attaches, as shown here:",
      "sourceHash": "3a14de562df109a340a9f57de2b636529e6d87bb37cc337f36015447feeaed57",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "The return type, [`Timer.TimerPublisher`](timer/timerpublisher.md), conforms to [`ConnectablePublisher`](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Combine/ConnectablePublisher), which means you must explicitly connect to the [`Timer`](timer.md) publisher to begin publishing events.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\ncancellable = Timer.publish(every: 1, on: .main, in: .common)\n    .autoconnect()\n    .sink() {\n        print (\"timer fired: \\($0)\")\n}\n\n```",
